P = Rs. 1800, C.I = Rs. 280.12, T = 2 years. Find the rate of interest per annum.
5%
6%
8%
7 1/2%
Solution:
Formula: A = P(1 + R/100)^T

Calculation:

A = P + CI = 1800 + 280.12 = Rs. 2080.12
(1 + R/100)² = 2080.12 / 1800 = 1.155622
1 + R/100 = √1.155622 ≈ 1.075
R/100 = 0.075, so R = 7.5%

Check with R = 7½%:

Year 1: 1800 × 0.075 = 135, so amount = 1935
Year 2: 1935 × 0.075 = 145.125, so amount = 2080.125
CI = 2080.125 − 1800 ≈ 280.12 ✓

The correct option is 7½%.
